Changelog: 15-10-2026 04:06:38

__version__ equals VERSION again (0.1.1): the release left it at 0.1.0, as the comment after it hid it from tools/check_versions.py and from Suite Releases' bump. The comment is gone, as in the other apps. The 0.1.1 release reports itself as 0.1.0 in its window and --version.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 03:27:56

Release 0.1.1.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:31:31

No translations (owner's decision): core's create_app() no longer takes lang, and AppInfo no longer has languages; the app was English only already and stays so.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:18:10

A relative path on the command line works: bazzite-pkgxtractor game.pkg and bazzite-pkgxtractor-cli game.pkg out, typed in ~/Downloads, mean ~/Downloads/game.pkg and ~/Downloads/out. The launchers changed into the app folder, so such a path pointed into the app instead. They now stay in the folder they are started from; python takes the package and its bundled bc250_core from the app folder all the same (install.sh's RUN_MODULE, which puts the app folder first on sys.path where python -m put the current folder). The window makes the package's path absolute before it loads it or hands it to an open window, which runs in another folder. File dialogs without a remembered folder (Compare Extractions, a first Browse) open in the folder the app was started from, the home folder from the menu, instead of the app folder. The installer test runs both launchers from another folder with a look-alike package in it.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:10:51

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:01:27

The app is on bc250_core (owner's decision, for consistency with the suite's apps): INFO (AppInfo) in __init__, core's create_app and exec_app in __main__ (the same names, Fusion style, icon and SIGTERM handling; core's rounded tooltips and the Inter title font are new), core's single instance, the first line built with AppHeader, and the settings opened with open_settings (the same ~/.config/bazzite-pkgxtractor/bazzite-pkgxtractor.ini). A second launch with a package (the menu entry or the terminal) loads it in the open window through open_pkg(), which the package given at start-up and a drop also use. install.sh bundles bc250_core from the suite checkout like the other core apps; a release has it bundled. --version names the core. Tests: the package given at start-up or by a later launch.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 16:43:50

Renamed without the bc250 prefix (owner's decision): the app is "Bazzite pkgxtractor", its app id bazzite-pkgxtractor and its package bazzite_pkgxtractor. So the launchers are ~/.local/bin/bazzite-pkgxtractor and bazzite-pkgxtractor-cli, the app lives in ~/.local/share/bazzite-pkgxtractor, its settings in ~/.config/bazzite-pkgxtractor/bazzite-pkgxtractor.ini, and the icons are images/bazzite-pkgxtractor.png and -128.png. Settings and logs of an earlier install under the old name are not carried over.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 16:34:11

The version starts at 0.1.0, like every app of the suite (owner's decision): VERSION and __version__ go from 1.0.0 to 0.1.0, before the first release.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 16:15:38

The app is part of the BC250 Bazzite Suite, as apps/bazzite-pkgxtractor, listed in the portal under "Development only". Its manual is the suite manual's chapter docs/apps/bazzite-pkgxtractor.md (bundled in a release as MANUAL.md); the README links to it. The files of the standalone repository went to the suite: CLAUDE.md (the porting notes and where the work stands are in the suite's MIGRATION.md), test.sh, tools/check_versions.py and tools/fix-modes.sh (the suite's own do the same), and .gitattributes (the suite's root one is the same file). The installer and the code are unchanged.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 11:25:00

The name of the console and its maker appear nowhere in the app, the manual, the installer or the tests (owner's decision): the app extracts "package (.pkg) files" for shadPS4; only the emulator's name keeps its letters.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 11:15:00

The comparison tools of the C++ repository's scripts/ folder, which the C++ GUI could only run as external Python scripts, are part of the app: compare_extractions.py was already built in as compare.py; compare_report_delta.py is now compare_delta.py (python -m bazzite_pkgxtractor.compare_delta before.json after.json [--out]). The Compare Extractions button opens a menu with both: "Compare two extraction folders…" and "Delta between two compare reports…", the latter logging the before/after summary and writing <after report>_delta.txt next to the after report. Tests for both modules and the window's delta flow; the manual describes them.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 11:05:00

The app is its own repository, github.com/RobertoTorino/bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor, named like the other standalone BC250 Bazzite apps: the app is "BC250 Bazzite pkgxtractor" (app id bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor, package bc250_pkgxtractor), installed to ~/.local/share/bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor with the launchers bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor and bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor-cli, its settings in ~/.config/bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor/bc250-bazzite-pkgxtractor.ini. The window has the suite's first line: the logo at 96 px beside the title with the version, the PKG file row below it. Added the manual (MARKDOWN.md), CLAUDE.md with the standing rules and where the work stands, test.sh, tools/check_versions.py and tools/fix-modes.sh as in the suite, and the suite's .gitattributes (every text file LF on both systems).

Changelog: 14-10-2026 10:40:00

Restructured after the owner's example app (bc250-bazzite-suite/apps/hdmi-cec): a flat package run with python -m, PyQt6 instead of PySide6, requirements.txt and VERSION instead of pyproject, install.sh with --uninstall/--purge/--no-desktop-shortcut installing into ~/.local/share/<app-id>/app with its own venv, images/<app-id>.png and -128.png, SPDX headers on every file, tests/conftest.py with an offscreen QApplication and settings in a temp folder. The Flatpak manifest and the separate .desktop file went with it.

Changelog: 14-10-2026 09:30:00

First Python + Qt port of pkgxtractor for Bazzite. The PKG/PFS/PSF parsing, the key derivation (RSA-PKCS1v15 in plain Python, AES-CBC, AES-XTS and HMAC through the cryptography package) and the GUI workflow (icon and param.sfo preview, rename to CONTENT_ID, preview-only, salvage mode, log file, crash marker and progress checkpoint) are ports of the C++ sources in github.com/RobertoTorino/pkgxtractor; the compare tool (scripts/compare_extractions.py there) is built in. Two findings while porting: the param.sfo format field is read little-endian (the C++ reads the big-endian field with .Raw()), and the PFS seed sits in the unencrypted first sector of the image. Verified against 22 real DLC packages (the full key chain: the decrypted license.dat carries the RIF magic and the content id) and a synthetic, properly encrypted game package with raw, compressed, multi-block and empty files (tests/pkg_builder.py).
